# Toronto farmers’ markets by day of the week

Looking for a farmers’ market **today**, tomorrow, or on a specific weekday? Here’s our take on Toronto and nearby published markets, grouped Monday through Sunday — hours and seasons from [MarketRegular](https://www.marketregular.com). Tap a name for the live listing, or jump straight to [markets open today](https://www.marketregular.com/markets/open-today) and the day filters ([Monday](https://www.marketregular.com/markets/day/monday) · [Tuesday](https://www.marketregular.com/markets/day/tuesday) · [Wednesday](https://www.marketregular.com/markets/day/wednesday) · [Thursday](https://www.marketregular.com/markets/day/thursday) · [Friday](https://www.marketregular.com/markets/day/friday) · [Saturday](https://www.marketregular.com/markets/day/saturday) · [Sunday](https://www.marketregular.com/markets/day/sunday)).

Seasons and hours shift — always confirm on the live page before you go. Lineups rotate; empty vendor counts on a listing mean the roster is still being filled, not that the hours are fake.

---

## Week at a glance

| Day | What to expect |
|---|---|
| **Monday** | Sorauren (park or winter indoor at Henderson) — the uncommon Monday slot |
| **Tuesday** | Morning East York + SickKids; afternoon Cabbagetown, Bellwoods, Davisville, Scarborough |
| **Wednesday** | Midweek Annex / Junction / Danforth / Malvern cluster |
| **Thursday** | Underpass, Dufferin Grove (year-round), East Lynn, North York morning |
| **Friday** | Fewer options — Thorncliffe and Warden Woods |
| **Saturday** | Biggest day — North farmers’ market from 5 AM, Brick Works, Withrow, Allan Gardens, Junction, The Stop |
| **Sunday** | Leslieville outdoor (in season), Eglinton Way early, Little Jamaica later, Deeply Rooted |

**Permanent hall, not a farmers’ market:** [St. Lawrence Market (South)](https://www.marketregular.com/markets/st-lawrence-market) runs most weekdays and Sunday with specialty merchants. The **Saturday farmers’ market** is [North](https://www.marketregular.com/markets/st-lawrence-farmers-market) only (5 AM–3 PM). Don’t mix the two.

